+src/index.ts            cordis plugin entry (volatile config schema, profile-entry
+                        settings writes, stats wiring)
 src/routes.ts           route-family aggregator (wraps every domain handler in the shared fences)
 src/routes/             one file per domain + shared layers:
                         http.ts (fences/JSON/error mapping), deps.ts (route deps + writable-skill
@@ -39,10 +40,17 @@ src/client/locales/     dictionaries by view (common/skills/market/sources/detai
 ```bash
 npm install
 npm run typecheck   # tsc --noEmit
-npm test            # vitest (253 tests across 14 suites)
+npm test            # vitest (261 tests across 15 suites)
 npm run build       # tsc declarations + tsdown bundles (lib/index.js + lib/client.js)
 ```
 
+The DSH packages are pinned exactly (prerelease cohort) in `devDependencies`, and
+`.npmrc` sets `legacy-peer-deps=true` because those prereleases' own peer ranges
+resolve to later prereleases of the same cohort. Runtime packages come from the
+`dsh` profile tree; the browser bundle externalises exactly the shell's shared
+module table (`PLATFORM_MODULES` in `tsdown.config.ts`) and must be re-checked
+against `@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-web/src/platform.ts` on every DSH upgrade.
+
